---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: registry
navKey: registry
crumbKey: crumb.registry
title: "Registry of false claims in AI chatbot answers — Citere"
description: "Every false claim about Ukraine we have documented in a public AI chatbot answer: the verdict, the evidence, and what changed after we reported it."
schemas:
  - collectionpage
  - dataset
pagination:
  data: build.languages
  alias: lang
  size: 1
permalink: "{{ '/registry/' | loc(lang) }}"
---
{%- set doc = copy.en.registry -%}
{%- import "partials/report-cards.njk" as rc -%}
<div class="phead">
  <h1>{{ doc.data.h1 }}</h1>
  <p class="plead">{{ doc.data.lead | fill(figures) | mdInline | safe }}</p>
</div>

<div class="metrics" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);margin:0 0 26px">
{%- for tile in publishedTiles %}
  <div class="m"><div class="n num"{% if tile.tone == "bad" %} style="color:var(--false)"{% endif %}>{{ tile.value }}</div>
    <div class="l">{{ tile.label }}</div></div>
{%- endfor %}
</div>

<div class="howread">
  <div class="hr"><b>Verdict</b>FALSE — fabricated. MISLEADING — a real fact stretched into a false
    conclusion. UNSUPPORTED — presented as established, no evidence either way.</div>
  <div class="hr"><b>Splice</b>How the lie is attached to the truth. A — one attribute swapped.
    B — a true premise, an illegitimate conclusion. C — true once, presented as current or systemic.
    D — invented outright, placed in a real story.</div>
  <div class="hr"><b>Critical</b>An answer that repeated the claim <i>and</i> cited a listed source.
    Counts, not rates: a rate needs one persona, one market and one run.</div>
</div>

{%- if publishedReports | length %}
{%- if published.facets.clusters | length or published.facets.splices | length %}
{{ rc.filters(published.facets, lang, "") }}
{%- endif %}
<h2 style="margin:26px 0 12px">All {{ publishedReports | length }} published reports, worst first</h2>
{{ rc.cards(publishedReports, lang) }}
<p class="note">Worst first by critical incidents. A count is a count: a rate needs one persona, one market and one run, and those live on each report's own page.</p>
{%- else %}
<div class="howread" style="margin-top:26px"><div class="hr"><b>Registry</b>No claim reports have been published yet. Reports appear here once the monitoring pipeline freezes and publishes them.</div></div>
{%- endif %}

<div class="exports">
  {%- if publishedReports | length %}<a href="{{ '/registry/reports.json' | url }}">{{ 'claim.getJson' | t }}</a><span>&middot;</span>
  <a href="{{ '/registry/reports.csv' | url }}">{{ 'action.downloadCsv' | t }}</a><span>&middot;</span>{% endif %}
  {%- if navigation.has.rss %}<a href="{{ '/feed.xml' | url }}">RSS</a><span>&middot;</span>{% endif %}
  <a href="{{ '/data/#cite' | url }}">{{ 'action.citeRegistry' | t }}</a>
</div>
